WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.177
Poor Geppetto was locked in prison.

2
00:00:03.178 --> 00:00:06.142
But Pinocchio was laughing and running through the forest.

3
00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:09.519
Pinocchio wasn’t wearing clothes, and he didn’t care.

4
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.426
"I’m free, I’m free," he shouted as he ran.

5
00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:18.877
"I can run and leap and play!"

6
00:00:18.878 --> 00:00:22.067
The sun began to set, and Pinocchio was getting tired.

7
00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:24.332
So he returned to Geppetto’s house.

8
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:28.487
"I’m hungry," he said, and he searched the house for food.

9
00:00:28.488 --> 00:00:34.151
But Pinocchio didn’t know how to cook, so he couldn’t eat.

10
00:00:34.152 --> 00:00:38.888
"I’m cold," he said, and he searched the house for clothes.

11
00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:42.726
But Pinocchio had run away before Geppetto could make him any clothes.

12
00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:44.984
So he wrapped himself in a blanket.

13
00:00:44.985 --> 00:00:52.263
"I’m tired," he said, but Geppetto’s bed was too tall.

14
00:00:52.264 --> 00:00:58.204
"Whaaa!" Pinocchio cried.

15
00:00:58.205 --> 00:01:05.967
"I am cold and hungry and tired, and there is no one here to take care of me!"

16
00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.905
Big tears ran down his wooden face.

17
00:01:08.906 --> 00:01:16.102
"Well, if you hadn’t been a bad boy, Geppetto would be here," said a tiny voice.

18
00:01:16.103 --> 00:01:20.153
"Who’s there?" asked Pinocchio, a little scared.

19
00:01:20.154 --> 00:01:22.655
Night was falling and the room was getting dark.

20
00:01:22.656 --> 00:01:24.887
Pinocchio couldn’t see anyone.

21
00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:29.054
"I am," said the voice again, with a chirping sound.

22
00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:32.852
A small candle on the table suddenly lit up.

23
00:01:32.853 --> 00:01:36.910
Pinocchio saw a cricket crawling down the candle.

24
00:01:36.911 --> 00:01:41.802
"Oh! You’re a bug!" said Pinocchio. "Who are you?"

25
00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:44.364
"My name is Mick the Cricket.

26
00:01:44.365 --> 00:01:46.867
You may call me Mr. Cricket.

27
00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:50.302
I have lived in this room for one hundred years.

28
00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:55.929
But I have never seen such a bad boy as you!" he scolded.

29
00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.428
"I don’t like you either!" said Pinocchio.

30
00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:02.549
He was mad at the cricket for calling him a bad boy.

31
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:06.351
"Shame on you for being rude!" chirped the cricket.

32
00:02:06.352 --> 00:02:11.287
"I am trying to help you, and Geppetto has been very kind.

33
00:02:11.288 --> 00:02:14.302
Is this how you thank your friends?

34
00:02:14.303 --> 00:02:17.805
If so, you will have very bad friends.

35
00:02:17.806 --> 00:02:22.066
Children should honor their parents, and you have not!"

36
00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.641
Pinocchio banged his hand on the table.

37
00:02:24.642 --> 00:02:28.316
He was trying to squash Mr. Cricket!

38
00:02:28.317 --> 00:02:29.637
"I’ll show you!

39
00:02:29.638 --> 00:02:33.961
I can have all the friends I want!" Pinocchio screamed.

40
00:02:33.962 --> 00:02:36.489
"I can do whatever I want!

41
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.022
I don’t have to honor anyone!

42
00:02:39.023 --> 00:02:41.996
I am going to go on adventures.

43
00:02:41.997 --> 00:02:45.581
One day, I will be rich and famous!"

44
00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:48.403
Mr. Cricket jumped to the floor to run away.

45
00:02:48.404 --> 00:02:52.281
But Pinocchio chased him and tried to step on him.

46
00:02:52.282 --> 00:02:56.139
"You are making very bad choices!" said the cricket.

47
00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.227
"One day those bad choices will hurt you.

48
00:02:59.228 --> 00:03:02.509
You can’t run away from the choices you’ve made.

49
00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:07.201
You must learn to do honest work and study to be a good boy,"

50
00:03:07.202 --> 00:03:12.452
he chirped, and he ran toward the door.

51
00:03:12.453 --> 00:03:15.333
"I won’t work. I won’t study.

52
00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:18.167
I won’t listen to what you say!

53
00:03:18.168 --> 00:03:23.039
I will do only what I want!" Pinocchio screamed.

54
00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.369
Mr. Cricket ran under the door.

55
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.339
Pinocchio kicked the door.

56
00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:35.536
He walked over to the table, sat down, and started to cry.

57
00:03:35.537 --> 00:03:41.403
"I won’t listen to you or anyone else," he cried.

58
00:03:41.404 --> 00:03:52.123
He fell asleep with teardrops dripping off his nose.

